# Comprehensive Educational Walkthrough: Mr. Robot CTF Lab
A deeply detailed, step-by-step breakdown of the reconnaissance, credential exploitation, foothold generation, and privilege escalation vectors executed against the Mr. Robot vulnerable machine.

---

## 🛡️ Executive Summary & Core Methodology
This document serves as an instructional guide detailing the systematic compromise of the target system. The entire lifecycle is executed across five distinct phases, using standard Linux utility structures and specialized security assessment tools. 

The core learning objectives demonstrated include:
*   File architecture enumeration and wordlist optimization.
*   Bypassing default administrative boundaries via targeted parameter manipulation.
*   Establishing interactive web-based remote shells and process stabilization.
*   Cryptographic hash identification and lateral privilege migration.
*   Identifying and exploiting vulnerable system permissions via misconfigured Set Owner User ID (`SUID`) bits.

